Hi Frank, I think the following thread is useful: https://groups.google.com/d/msg/unmarked/VWJfixK6Z2k/RqHQDjrqd8cJ

Essentially yes, you could capture yearly variation with phi.  And if you are most interested in site covariates, it will probably work well enough.  A more explicit hierarchical model for multi-year distance sampling was recently described here:

Sollmann, R., B. Gardner, R. B. Chandler, J. A. Royle, and T. S. Sillett. 2015. An open-population hierarchical distance sampling model. Ecology 96:325-331.

